"1. Load MovieLens100K ratings from the local `u.data` file with the correct tab-separated schema: user, item, rating, timestamp.\n2. Use LensKit\u2019s ImplicitMF recommender as the sole model under study, with one fixed hyperparameter configuration reused across all runs.\n3. Perform a single 80/20 train/test split of the ratings data and keep that split fixed for all seed comparisons so only model randomness varies.\n4. Generate top-N recommendations for test users from models trained with different random seeds while holding all non-seed settings constant.\n5. Evaluate each run with ranking metrics appropriate for implicit recommendation, including at least NDCG and Recall at a clearly specified cutoff K.\n6. Repeat training and evaluation for multiple distinct random seeds (enough to estimate variability; e.g., 10+ runs).\n7. Record per-seed metric results and compute summary statistics across runs, including mean, standard deviation, min, and max for each metric.\n8. Quantify seed sensitivity by comparing metric dispersion across runs and report whether observed variation is practically meaningful relative to the metric scale.\n9. Ensure the evaluation protocol is conceptually consistent with ImplicitMF: define positive test interactions appropriately and exclude items seen in each user\u2019s training history from recommendation candidates.\n10. Make the experiment reproducible by explicitly setting and logging every seed used and by keeping data loading, split, model configuration, and evaluation settings deterministic aside from the model seed.\n11. Include code that prints or saves a concise results table of metrics by seed plus the aggregate variability summary.\n12. Handle users/items in the test set robustly so the evaluation runs without errors under LensKit\u2019s APIs."